Fixed. Here's what was wrong and what I did:

**Problem:** The `pip` package files had been deleted from `/usr/local/lib/python3.13/site-packages/`, but the `.dist-info` metadata directory (`pip-24.3.1.dist-info`) was still there. This left a dangling `pip3` binary that pointed to a missing `pip` module — `pip` thought it was installed (because of the metadata) but the actual code was gone.

**Fix:** I removed the orphaned `pip-24.3.1.dist-info` directory and re-ran `python3 -m ensurepip --default-pip`, which restored the full pip package. pip is now working again (`pip3 --version` confirms 24.3.1).

